# The Nuxt Worker owns no AI setting, no provider credential, and no D1 binding. A briefing submission crosses the
# private `BRIEFING_SERVICE` binding to the briefing Worker, which reads its own local settings from the git-ignored
# `workers/briefing/.dev.vars` beside its Wrangler config (or from a Worker secret when deployed). Nuxt still reads
# this `.env`, but none of the names below belong to it any more, and nothing is copied into `.output/server/.dev.vars`.

# Local fixture: point the three briefing-Worker settings at a loopback OpenAI-compatible endpoint and treat its output
# as a test double rather than inference. The values live in `workers/briefing/.dev.vars`, not here:
#   AI_BRIEFING_ENDPOINT="http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/chat/completions"
#   AI_BRIEFING_API_KEY="local-fixture-key"
#   AI_BRIEFING_MODEL="local-fixture-model"

# Real inference uses the same three names in the briefing Worker's environment. The endpoint is the complete
# OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions URL: its path must end with /chat/completions, and query parameters are rejected.
#   AI_BRIEFING_ENDPOINT=https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/chat/completions
#   AI_BRIEFING_API_KEY=<key>
#   AI_BRIEFING_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
# OpenRouter alternative: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions with deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash.

# Evidence provider credentials belong to the private evidence Worker: an optional GITHUB_TOKEN goes in
# `workers/evidence/.dev.vars` for local runs, or a secret on the deployed evidence Worker. Do not copy AI credentials
# there, and do not put a real provider key in this file.
